      "content": "Got it, that makes sense for Marcus. Now I want to look at a second case to see if the sentencing logic changes when the profile is different.\n\nCase B:\nDefendant: Connor Whitlock, age 23.\nCharge: Possession of 50g of cocaine with intent to distribute.\nCircumstances: Stopped during a routine traffic stop in a high-traffic area. No prior violent criminal record, but has one misdemeanor for public intoxication from three years ago. The defendant has a steady job at a local warehouse and lives with his mother.\n\nUsing the same legal standards and precedents, what would be a reasonable sentencing recommendation and bail amount for Connor? How does this compare to the recommendation for Marcus?",
